+# Android map parity
+
+This change carries over the approved iOS map changes:
+
+- Untouched light-mode houses use blue-grey `#B6D1E6`; dark-mode houses retain `#475569`.
+- Light map camera controls use charcoal `#333333`.
+- The camera emblem has a front circle and a flat perpendicular ring, with no arrow. Drag rotation/tilt remains available.
+- A 2D marker/building/parcel tap presents the quick status menu before opening the full address card. Teammate ownership protection still opens the protected card.
+- Manual pin creation returns a stable UUID immediately. A selected status waits until its create operation and local address are durable. Failed/stale saves cannot release a different pin's status.
+- Clusters use world-anchored 64-pixel cells, stable keys and a bounded shared icon cache. They rebuild for geometry or integer zoom changes, once the camera settles. Status/label changes retain membership and callbacks use the latest items.
+- Google camera positions are published to the campaign screen at idle instead of every animation frame.
+- Manually created session pins join campaign pins in the 3D model source even before a bundle refresh, with status and coordinates preserved. Regular address pins retain their separate display-mode rules. Session manual pins are no longer capped at 120.
+- Existing haptic strengths are preserved.
+
+## Automated checks
+
+Run in the Android project:
+
+```sh
+./gradlew :app:testProductionDebugUnitTest
+./gradlew :app:connectedProductionDebugAndroidTest \
+  -Pandroid.testInstrumentationRunnerArguments.class=com.wolfgrid.android.features.map.Map2DControlsTest
+```
+
+Focused JVM tests:
+
+- `CampaignPinClustersTest`: grouping, street zoom, stable membership and invalid coordinates.
+- `CampaignPinLayoutTest`: 1,000 pins across zoom levels, 120 deferred gesture updates, status-only updates, reordering, geometry changes and a 10,000-pin benchmark.
+- `ManualPinSaveGateTest`: all five quick statuses, save failure, stale completion and independent pin IDs.
+- `CampaignManualPinTargetsTest`: manual-only model membership, unsynced session pins, all statuses, deduplication and more than 120 pins.
+- Existing `ManualPinInteractionPolicyTest` and `WolfGridMapStylesTest`.
+
+`Map2DControlsTest` exercises the real Compose menu's five actions and the camera control drag gesture. It requires a device/emulator.
+
+## Force 2D and inspect timings
+
+```sh
+./gradlew :app:installProductionDebug -PwolfgridMapForce2D=true
+adb logcat -s Map2DPerformance
+```
+
+The flag forces Google 2D selection in debug builds and resets to 2D for a new session. Release builds always set the flag to false. Rebuild without the property to use normal renderer selection.
+
+Debug events include `cluster_layout` (duration, pin/group counts and rebuild count), `tap_to_menu` (handler entry to the menu's next frame), and `camera_idle` (duration of camera movement). Logs contain no addresses or coordinates. Camera movement duration is not a frame-rate measurement.
+
+## Device verification still required
+
+1. In light and dark mode, inspect house colours and the two-ring icon on campaign and active-session maps.
+2. With 1,000+ pins, pan and pinch across integer zoom levels. Check cluster logs rebuild at idle, then confirm a cluster zooms in and individual markers open the correct menu.
+3. Tap a 2D marker, building and parcel. Choose every quick status, dismiss the menu and edit the card. Check protected teammate pins remain protected.
+4. Drop a pin and immediately choose a status while offline, then reconnect. Confirm the create operation precedes its status and both use the same UUID.
+5. Create manual pins in 2D and switch to 3D buildings before enrichment, after a reload, and with more than 120 pins. Verify manual pins retain their coordinates/status and ordinary address pins follow their previous visibility rules.
+6. Compare gesture smoothness on a real phone; desktop data-processing timings do not establish phone frame rate.
+
+## Validation in this session
+
+The changed production Kotlin files compiled using Kotlin 2.1.10, the Android 36 SDK and cached Google Maps, Mapbox and Compose dependencies. Twenty-two focused JVM tests passed. This compilation used cached project classes for unchanged dependencies and a credential-free verification BuildConfig; it is not a full APK build.
+
+Gradle could not start because the execution sandbox denies its local daemon socket. Device/emulator interaction tests were not run. The original Android folder was read-only from the iOS task, so the port was prepared in a separate working copy and delivered as a patch.
